2026-02-01 23:53:15,855 - DocumentGraderNode - INFO: Retrieved document The Bottom Line

Normal distribution, also known as the Gaussian distribution, is a probability distribution that appears as a "bell curve" when graphed. The normal distribution describes a symmetrical plot of data around its mean value, where the width of the curve is defined by the standard deviation. is relevant
