The term Nasdaq is also used to refer to the Nasdaq Composite. This is an index of more than 2,500 stocks listed on the Nasdaq exchange. This index includes some of the major technology giants, such as:

- Apple (AAPL)
- Microsoft (MSFT)
- Alphabet (GOOG, GOOGL)
- Meta Platforms (META)
- Amazon (AMZN)
- Tesla (TSLA)

The Nasdaq Composite closed at a record high of 16,057.44 on Nov. 19, 2021. The index proceeded to drop more than 23% from that point through April 2022. The Nasdaq Composite's 13.3% drop in April 2022 was its steepest monthly decline since losing 17.4% in October 2008 during the global financial crisis. It closed at 13,787.92 on June 30, 2023. is relevant
